game challenge idea:

title: Solving Superstitions

short summary: start out in a cabin in the woods trying to prove stuff like bigfoot is real.
given a basic tutorial on how the game works by trying to get the player to get pictures of a squirrel and compile an article of your findings.
when they are actually in the game they need to first chose what monster they are trying to prove first.
there is an encyclopedia of all the available monsters which gives a description of where it might be located.
when the player sets out to find the monster there will be tracks like footprints.
once they find the monster they need to get atleast 2 pictures of it doing a different action(no copys of it doing the same thing).
the more unique pictures taken the greater the reward. maybe could try get some sort of sample too like big foot hair.
if the player is too close to the animal you get chased and reset.
once returned to base they can compile all of the photos together in a newspaper article and publish it.
publishing earns money and you can buy more tape for the camera with the money.
